        "value": "Conversion note set as a two-line half-width insert under the silver figure (right line 兩ニ付六, left line 拾錢替): the silver is reckoned at sixty monme to the ryō. 錢 here stands for the weight unit 匁, exactly as it does in the figure above, so the note records the standard rate of sixty monme of silver to one ryō of gold."
